      "text": "To find the values of \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) in the line equation \\(y = ax + b\\), we start by using the given points \\((4,5)\\) and \\((8,17)\\). These points satisfy the equation of the line, so we can substitute them into the equation separately.\n\nFor the point \\((4,5)\\):\n\\[5 = 4a + b \\quad \\text{(Equation 1)}\\]\n\nFor the point \\((8,17)\\):\n\\[17 = 8a + b \\quad \\text{(Equation 2)}\\]\n\nTo eliminate \\(b\\), we subtract Equation 1 from Equation 2:\n\\[\n17 - 5 = 8a + b - (4a + b)\n\\]\n\\[\n12 = 4a\n\\]\n\\[\na = \\frac{12}{4} = 3\n\\]\n\nNow that we have \\(a = 3\\), we substitute this value back into Equation 1 to find \\(b\\):\n\\[\n5 = 4(3) + b\n\\]\n\\[\n5 = 12 + b\n\\]\n\\[\nb = 5 - 12 = -7\n\\]\n\nSo, the slope \\(a\\) is 3 and the y-intercept \\(b\\) is -7. Therefore, the expression \\(a - b\\) is:\n\\[\na - b = 3 - (-7) = 3 + 7 = 10\n\\]\n\nThe final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{10}\n\\]",
